00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.880
If you make a great product

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.413
and you get people to taste
it, physically and literally,

00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:59.638
meaning try your app,
check out your store,

00:01:59.638 --> 00:02:03.860
wear your hoody, or actually
try sauce and it's delicious,

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.224
word of mouth will kick in.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.691
I think the world we live in now,

00:02:07.691 --> 00:02:08.836
it actually speeds that up

00:02:08.836 --> 00:02:10.283
because when somebody had that sauce,

00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:11.579
now they take a photo
and put on Instagram,

00:02:11.579 --> 00:02:13.032
be like, "This is delicious."

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.923
That's a lot better than 1997

00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:16.209
where, like, I had this sauce

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:17.852
and then, like, Staphon and
I are playing basketball,

00:02:17.852 --> 00:02:20.155
we go, "By the way, the sauce,"
like, what? I did that once?

00:02:20.155 --> 00:02:22.431
Like, I think it was impossible to amplify

00:02:22.431 --> 00:02:25.037
the way we are now on an
individual person level,

00:02:25.037 --> 00:02:27.554
so I actually think the era of companies

00:02:27.554 --> 00:02:32.247
with very limited or zero
marketing budgets is here

00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:35.458
and I do think social
media is that foundation.

00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:39.318
So, what interests me is that
this is the greatest time ever

00:02:39.318 --> 00:02:42.908
to not have a marketing budget
in a world as a marketer

00:02:42.908 --> 00:02:45.325
because so much of it can
be organic and authentic.

00:02:45.325 --> 00:02:47.109
It's hard, you have to be great,

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:51.081
and most of all, your product
has to be sensational.

00:02:51.081 --> 00:02:53.083
So I think the brands that will break out,

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:56.194
the products that will break
out in the next half decade

00:02:56.194 --> 00:02:59.234
with zero dollars are gonna be anomalies,

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.075
but that's predicated on them

00:03:01.075 --> 00:03:04.266
actually making a phenomenal product.

